== Trivia ==
* ''Purpur'' is a specific shade of purple in multiple languages, including Swedish, Polish, German, and Cornish (and French ''pourpre'').
* Mojang has associated purpur blocks with the expensive {{W|Tyrian purple|newtab=1}} dye of antiquity, made from the secretions of sea snails.<ref>{{cite|author=Alex Wiltshire
|date=28 April 2017 |title=Block of the Week: Pupur |url=https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/article/block-week-purpur |website=minecraft.net}}</ref>
* {{W|Purpurite|newtab=1}} is also a real-world manganese phosphate mineral that has a purple hue.

