A '''red shrub''' is a non-solid [[plant]] block found in [[dappled forest]]s. Red shrubs are not [[Biome tint|biome tinted]] like most other plants, keeping their red color regardless of the [[biome]] they are placed in.

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
A red shrub can be broken instantly with any item or by hand, dropping itself.

{{breaking row|horizontal=1|Red Shrub}}

A red shrub also breaks and drops itself if [[water]] runs over its location, a [[piston]] extends or pushes a block into its location, or the block under the plant is moved or destroyed. However, a red shrub gets destroyed without dropping anything if [[lava]] runs over it.

Placing any block on a red shrub replaces the shrub without dropping anything.

=== Natural generation ===
Red shrubs occasionally generate in patches in [[dappled forest]]s.

=== Post-generation ===
{{control|Using}} [[bone meal]] on a red shrub attempts to grow another red shrub on a horizontally/vertically neighboring block.

== Usage ==
Red shrubs are a decorative plant and can be placed on any of the following blocks:
{{columns-list|style=column-count:2|
* {{BlockLink|Grass Block}}
* {{BlockLink|Mycelium}}
* {{BlockLink|Podzol}}
* {{BlockLink|Dirt}}
* {{BlockLink|Coarse Dirt}}
* {{BlockLink|Rooted Dirt}}
* {{BlockLink|Farmland}}
* {{BlockLink|Mud}}
* {{BlockLink|Muddy Mangrove Roots}}
* {{BlockLink|Moss Block}}
* {{BlockLink|Pale Moss Block}}
}}

Unlike most plants, red shrubs cannot be placed inside [[flower pot]]s. They can be [[snowlogged]].{{Only|be|short=1}}

=== Composting ===
Placing a red shrub into a [[composter]] has a 30% chance of raising the compost level by 1.

